use an uninitialized buffer length variable with a zeroed buffer to be returned in fips mode. it may also be possible to force a false positive match between non-equal hashes when comparing a trusted computed hmac sum to an untrusted input sum if an attacker can send a zeroed buffer in place of a pre-computed sum.\u00a0 it is also possible to force a derived key to be all zeros instead of an unpredictable value.\u00a0 this may have follow-on implications for the go tls stack."},{"subject":"CVE-2024-9355","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 7 Extended Lifecycle Support","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat enterprise linux 7 extended lifecycle support"},{"subject":"CVE-2024-9355","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat enterprise linux 8"},{"subject":"CVE-2024-9355","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat enterprise linux 9"},{"subject":"CVE-2024-9355","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9.4 Extended Update Support","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat enterprise linux 9.4 extended update support"},{"subject":"CVE-2024-9355","predicate":"product","object":"Satellite Client 6 for RHEL 10","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"satellite client 6 for rhel 10"},{"subject":"CVE-2024-9355","predicate":"product","object":"Satellite Client 6 for RHEL 8","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"satellite client 6 for rhel 8"},{"subject":"CVE-2024-9355","predicate":"product","object":"Satellite Client 6 for RHEL 9","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"satellite client 6 for rhel 9"},{"subject":"CVE-2024-9355","predicate":"product","object":"Streams for Apache Kafka 2.9.0","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"streams for apache kafka